h is an overcard to your pair. The opponent showed passivity by checking pre-flop and checking the flop. While you have showdown value, your hand is not strong enough to comfortably build a large pot, and you are vulnerable to overcards and flush draws.\n\nReason: Checking is the best option here to control the size of the pot ("pot control"). Betting might force out worse hands that you are beating while only getting action from hands that beat you (like a Queen or a better 8). By checking, you can potentially catch a bluff on later streets or get to a cheap showdown.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
