ng kicker can take it down.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: The opponent has checked on the Flop, Turn, and River, indicating a very weak hand or a desire to reach showdown cheaply. Your hand is a Pair of 6s with a King kicker (K, Q, 9, 6, 6). This effectively functions as King-high beating other high-card hands, but losing to Ace-high or any pocket pair. Given the passive line, your hand has significant showdown value. Betting is unlikely to get called by worse hands (like J-high) and might not fold out better hands (like A-high) consistently. Since you are in the lead overall, minimizing variance by checking back is the optimal strategy.\n\nReason: You have a made hand (Pair of 6s, King kicker) with reasonable showdown value against a passive opponent. Checking avoids the risk of being check-raised or betting into a better hand while realizing your equity for free.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
